         "title": "Rui Miranda: “When I was 12 years old I wanted to have my own bank. I wanted to have something of my own”",
         "description": "<p><span>From corporate boardrooms to the global animation stage, Rui Miranda has spent two decades betting on himself. The former Procter & Gamble and TVI executive, who brought Big Brother to Portuguese television, is now releasing the highest-budget animated film ever made in Portugal. Speaking on “The Heart & Hustle” podcast, Miranda traced the path from a 12-year-old who dreamed of owning a bank to an independent producer with 60 countries on his client list.</span></p>",
